[1] JACOBIAN CHECK  (u-coordinate  vs  x = cos u)
==============================================================================
substitution: x=cos u  =>  du = -dx/sqrt(1-x^2),  sin^2 u = 1-x^2
  sin^2u/u du = (1-x^2)/u * du = (1-x^2)/u * (-dx/sqrt(1-x^2))
              = -sqrt(1-x^2)/arccos(x) dx   [orientation flip: u:0->pi  <=>  x:1->-1]
  => int_0^pi h(u) du = int_{-1}^{1} h(arccos x) * w(x) dx,
     w(x) = sqrt(1-x^2)/arccos x  (= 2g(x), w(1)=1, w(-1)=0)
  => nu_c ~ e^{-beta} * e^{beta c x} w(x) dx   : exponential family in x, natural par. beta*c

